I assume the problem is that it's a new fuzzer, and that it will
fix itself when it's merged. I suggest to ignore it.

I've been running it with the following patch applied:
--- a/fuzz/cmp.c
+++ b/fuzz/cmp.c
@@ -15,9 +15,14 @@
 #include <openssl/cmp.h>
 #include <openssl/err.h>
 #include "fuzzer.h"
+#include "rand.inc"

 int FuzzerInitialize(int *argc, char ***argv)
 {
+    OPENSSL_init_crypto(OPENSSL_INIT_LOAD_CRYPTO_STRINGS, NULL);
+    ERR_clear_error();
+    CRYPTO_free_ex_index(0, -1);
+    FuzzerSetRand();
     return 1;
 }

@@ -50,6 +55,7 @@ int FuzzerTestOneInput(const uint8_t *buf, size_t len)
         OSSL_CMP_CTX *client_ctx = OSSL_CMP_CTX_new();

         i2d_OSSL_CMP_MSG_bio(out, msg);
+        ASN1_item_print(out, (ASN1_VALUE *)msg, 4, ASN1_ITEM_rptr(OSSL_CMP_MSG), NULL);
         BIO_free(out);

         if (client_ctx != NULL)

And currently get:
#13522  INITED cov: 5852 ft: 20834 corp: 2428/1317Kb exec/s: 540 rss: 586Mb

I merged the existing files from the test suite, which greatly
increased the coverage. The fuzzer has found a lot of new coverage
(cov), covering a lot of new function since I've added the samples
from the test suite. If you can share more real files, I would love
to merge them too.

I'm not sure FUZZING_BUILD_MODE_UNSAFE_FOR_PRODUCTION is needed, I
think the fuzzer can actually find the correct input. It is at
least finding lots of inputs without it.
